    {
      "filename": "Ford Highland Park Manufacturing Plant and strip mall, Highland Park, Michigan - 20201213.jpg",
      "title": "File:Ford Highland Park Manufacturing Plant and strip mall, Highland Park, Michigan - 20201213.jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/88/Ford_Highland_Park_Manufacturing_Plant_and_strip_mall%2C_Highland_Park%2C_Michigan_-_20201213.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ford_Highland_Park_Manufacturing_Plant_and_strip_mall,_Highland_Park,_Michigan_-_20201213.jpg",
      "width": 2645,
      "height": 1486,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0",
      "artist": "Andre Carrotflower",
      "description": "As seen in December 2020: the glorious past and banal present of Highland Park are both on display as we see a modern-day strip mall (anchored by discount retailers such as Rainbow, CitiTrends, and Super Dollar Center) along Woodward Avenue with the sprawling Ford Highland Park Manufacturing Plant, birthplace of the famous Model T, rising in the background.",
